[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2629516092","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102290#issuecomment-2629516092","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102290","id":2629516092,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cuzs8","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-02T19:05:05Z","updated_at":"2025-02-02T19:05:05Z","body":"I can't reproduce the issue with 4.3 stable on an M2 MBP. There is a good chance this is a hardware specific issue. `dFdy` and `dFdx` have hardware-specific implementations and their behaviour can vary drastically depending on whether the driver uses \"coarse\" or \"fine\" derivatives. IIRC NVidia defaults to coarse derivatives which means `dFdy` is basically shorthand for `dFdyCoarse`. For something like what you are doing, you need the fine derivative, so you should probably be using `dFdyFine` instead. Could you try that and see if it improves the output for you?\n\n\n_Screenshot of the MRP on my device_\n<img width=\"596\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/82750209-36d3-4073-b11a-663eecb99a2d\" />","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2629516092/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2629553310","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102290#issuecomment-2629553310","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102290","id":2629553310,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cu8ye","user":{"login":"ThePywon","id":79721537,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5NzIxNTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/79721537?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon","html_url":"https://github.com/ThePywon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-02T21:01:01Z","updated_at":"2025-02-02T21:28:31Z","body":"@clayjohn I promise you this is not a hardware issue, doing the same thing but with `VERTEX` data for example does not cause any issue.\n\nA friend of mine has tested it on linux without finding a problem themself as well.\nHave you tried Win11 Vulkan (Mobile)?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2629553310/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2629555047","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102290#issuecomment-2629555047","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102290","id":2629555047,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cu9Nn","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-02T21:05:49Z","updated_at":"2025-02-02T21:05:49Z","body":"First try using fine derivatives. This looks exactly like what I would expect from using coarse derivatives. \n\nBy hardware issue I don't mean to say that your hardware is somehow _broken_, I'm saying that the behaviour of this function depends on what hardware you use. Which is exactly how dFdy is supposed to work: https://registry.khronos.org/OpenGL-Refpages/gl4/html/dFdx.xhtml\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2629555047/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2629561539","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102290#issuecomment-2629561539","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102290","id":2629561539,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cu-zD","user":{"login":"ThePywon","id":79721537,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5NzIxNTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/79721537?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon","html_url":"https://github.com/ThePywon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-02T21:26:06Z","updated_at":"2025-02-02T21:26:06Z","body":"I have, and just tried it once again to be sure, same exact result.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/aad6e67c-21e0-4c6d-8a42-a7d5afebee4b)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2629561539/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2629602725","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102290#issuecomment-2629602725","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102290","id":2629602725,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cvI2l","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-02T23:03:29Z","updated_at":"2025-02-02T23:03:29Z","body":"Ooooh thanks for the screenshot. Your shader code is different than the MRP. \n\nI think the problem most likely comes from `n_pos`. You are calculating a derivative with `fwidth` then using that to select between two values, then taking the derivative of the selected value. \n\nThe trouble is GPUs calculate derivatives by sampling a neighbouring pixel in the quad. If each pixel takes a different path down your branch, then you end up with nonsensical derivatives. \n\nYou should only branch between values that will be used as an input to a derivate of you can guarantee that the value will stay the same for the entire pixel quad. Otherwise you end up with invalid values","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2629602725/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2629668743","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102290#issuecomment-2629668743","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102290","id":2629668743,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cvY-H","user":{"login":"ThePywon","id":79721537,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5NzIxNTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/79721537?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon","html_url":"https://github.com/ThePywon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-03T00:49:25Z","updated_at":"2025-02-03T00:49:25Z","body":"Right, here is the same thing with the MRP.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7f502f19-effd-4770-a46e-ab61aa0d3c67)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2629668743/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2629679743","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102290#issuecomment-2629679743","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102290","id":2629679743,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cvbp_","user":{"login":"Caznix","id":131402549,"node_id":"U_kgDOB9ULNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131402549?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caznix","html_url":"https://github.com/Caznix","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caznix/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caznix/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caznix/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caznix/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caznix/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caznix/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caznix/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caznix/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Caznix/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-03T01:04:57Z","updated_at":"2025-02-03T01:04:57Z","body":"> I can't reproduce the issue with 4.3 stable on an M2 MBP. There is a good chance this is a hardware specific issue. `dFdy` and `dFdx` have hardware-specific implementations and their behaviour can vary drastically depending on whether the driver uses \"coarse\" or \"fine\" derivatives. IIRC NVidia defaults to coarse derivatives which means `dFdy` is basically shorthand for `dFdyCoarse`. For something like what you are doing, you need the fine derivative, so you should probably be using `dFdyFine` instead. Could you try that and see if it improves the output for you?\n> \n> _Screenshot of the MRP on my device_ <img alt=\"Image\" width=\"596\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/16521339/408891472-82750209-36d3-4073-b11a-663eecb99a2d.png?jwt=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..huXJAs25VEgHkC7Qgx2bZJ8nHKgNm_ae-u9w-AVXhkg\">\n\nI was able to reproduce this with the MRP on my Linux system. If requested i can try booting into windows to verify there as well.\n\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4fd0a96c-019e-48c7-a897-57f108c0e5bc)\n\nMy systems specifications are as follows:\n\nGodot v4.3.stable (77dcf97d8) - cpe:/o:nixos:nixos:25.05 #1-NixOS SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Thu Jan 23 16:23:05 UTC 2025 - Wayland - Vulkan (Mobile) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3080 Laptop GPU - 11th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-11900H @ 2.50GHz (16 Threads)\n\nto be clear, this is using the mobile renderer","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2629679743/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2629693776","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102290#issuecomment-2629693776","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102290","id":2629693776,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cvfFQ","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-03T01:21:57Z","updated_at":"2025-02-03T01:33:01Z","body":"Thanks for double checking with the MRP! Can you check with `dFdxFine`, again? `dFdxCoarse` is not going to give you the behaviour you want, and that is what NVidia defaults to (if I am remembering correctly)\n\nI have tested on another device and still can't reproduce the issue. Which, again, is no surprise as this is likely NVidia-specific behaviour. \n\nThis time I tested on a Popos device with an intel integrated GPU. Intel doesn't do `dFdxCoarse`, it always uses fine derivatives\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0627127a-cf8e-4dd5-a43d-f74356febf39)\n\n Finally, I've tested on a Windows 10 device with an RX 6900 XT and it also looks fine with the MRP. So we can pretty conclusively say that this is NVidia specific behaviour\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e8e9020e-f3d7-4f3f-9bff-1211df0cd6ca)\n\nTo be clear, Godot has no control over what the GPU does with your shader code. For the most part, Godot leaves your shader code alone and just passes it off to the GPU driver. That is why I am so quick to point to issues in your code (undefined behaviour is always bad, even when it appears to work fine on your machine), and to ambiguity in the specification. \n\nAlso, I just noticed now, in your last screenshot you used `dFdxFine` and `dFdyFine`, but you forgot to use `fwidthFine`, so you are still using coarse derivatives for `fwidth`. For your original shader, you definitely want to use fine derivatives, and you need to get rid of the undefined behaviour otherwise you are setting yourself up for pain in the future","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2629693776/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2631059444","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102290#issuecomment-2631059444","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102290","id":2631059444,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6c0sf0","user":{"login":"ThePywon","id":79721537,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5NzIxNTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/79721537?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon","html_url":"https://github.com/ThePywon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThePywon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-03T13:49:38Z","updated_at":"2025-02-03T14:04:59Z","body":"I can assure you that my specs default to fine, but to be absolutely certain I have tried it once more.\nAs for whether or not it is nvidia specific, I have a hunch you are right (I know @Caznix, they have NVIDIA), which is pretty unfortunate to say the least, but at least I can point people to this issue in order to explain the reason behind the artefacts.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/31b578e9-2eed-49b4-9a31-adc809699d33)\n\n![Image](https://github.com/